            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I've tested this setup with Python and it works for me:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n  require('mini.ai').setup({\r\n    custom_textobjects = {\r\n      u = require('mini.ai').gen_spec.treesitter({ a = '@class.outer', i = '@class.outer' }),\r\n    },\r\n  })\r\n```\r\n\r\nMy guess is that this is a result of conflicting mapping(s) for `au`/`iu` which gets triggered instead of `a` and `i` defined by 'mini.ai'. Could you execute `:xmap a`, `:xmap i`, `:omap a`, `:omap i` and see if there are `au`/`iu` mappings that don't come from 'mini.ai'? If yes, then you have two options:\r\n- Delete them.\r\n- Type `a`/`i` and wait at least `timeoutlen` milliseconds and only then type `u`.",
