            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Thanks for a quick response @echasnovski. I checked my `:xmap` and `omap` mappings and `u` is not mapped to anything. Here is my `omap` output. `xmap` looks very similar:\r\n```\r\n   <Space>     * <Cmd>lua require(\"packer.load\")({'which-key.nvim'}, { keys = \"<leader>\", prefix = \"\" }, _G.packer_plugins)<CR>\r\no  al            v:lua.MiniAi.expr_textobject('o', 'a', {'search_method': 'prev'})\r\n                 Around last textobject\r\no  an            v:lua.MiniAi.expr_textobject('o', 'a', {'search_method': 'next'})\r\n                 Around next textobject\r\no  a             v:lua.MiniAi.expr_textobject('o', 'a')\r\n                 Around textobject\r\n   gc          * <Cmd>lua require(\"packer.load\")({'Comment.nvim'}, { keys = \"gc\", prefix = \"\" }, _G.packer_plugins)<CR>\r\n   gb          * <Cmd>lua require(\"packer.load\")({'Comment.nvim'}, { keys = \"gb\", prefix = \"\" }, _G.packer_plugins)<CR>\r\no  g]            v:lua.MiniAi.expr_motion('right')\r\n                 Move to right \"around\"\r\no  g[            v:lua.MiniAi.expr_motion('left')\r\n                 Move to left \"around\"\r\no  il            v:lua.MiniAi.expr_textobject('o', 'i', {'search_method': 'prev'})\r\n                 Inside last textobject\r\no  in            v:lua.MiniAi.expr_textobject('o', 'i', {'search_method': 'next'})\r\n                 Inside next textobject\r\no  i             v:lua.MiniAi.expr_textobject('o', 'i')\r\n                 Inside textobject\r\n   <Plug>luasnip-expand-repeat * <Cmd>lua require'luasnip'.expand_repeat()<CR>\r\n   <Plug>luasnip-delete-check * <Cmd>lua require'luasnip'.unlink_current_if_deleted()<CR>\r\n```\r\n\r\nI can test with a python project and let you know. One observation is that none of the custom textobject mappings show up in the `omap` output, but others are working.",
