        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Oh, it does work for me. With one little change (and in some cases without it).\r\n\r\nBy any chance, does it give a following message in the command line: `` No textobject \"au\" found covering region within 50 lines and `search_method = 'cover_or_next'`. ``? Basically, it means what it says: it couldn't find textobject with those parameters listed. It is meant as indication that at least *one* of those should be changed.\r\n\r\nIn your case, it is a `50 lines` part. Both 'mini.ai' and 'mini.surround' work by fetching some neighborhood of initial (reference) region and performing search within those. For speed and certain usability reasons, 'mini.ai' uses 50 lines before start and after end of reference region. In case of your example, target class region spans 84 lines, so if you put your cursor near its edges it can't find it. But if you place cursor on line 75 and it should select that region.\r\n\r\nIf you don't want this behavior, set `config.n_lines` to some very high value (like 10000). It will come at a cost of somewhat increased execution time. Still should be unnoticeable and very quick though. ",
